{"Using `timezone.now()` directly as the field default means it is evaluated once at import time and all future AssignmentSource instances will carry the same timestamp, so the queued field will never reflect when a particular assignment was actually queued. Should use `default_factory=timezone.now` instead.": 0.9673537015914917, "AssignmentSource.to_dict() includes a raw datetime in the queued field, but assignment_source_dict is passed to apply_async which requires JSON-serializable data. Celery's JSON serializer will raise TypeError. Need to serialize queued to ISO 8601 string when emitting the dict and parse it back in from_dict.": 0.9571875333786011}